   "notes": "Queens' College, long Tudor red-brick range on the north side of Silver Street (towards the Queens' Lane corner turret): two storeys plus a row of tile-hung dormers in the old tile roof and tall chimney stacks; stone plinth, stone-dressed windows: small square mullioned lights on the ground floor, a few arched/pointed two-light windows on the first floor, and a blocked stone window surround; quoined corner turret at the east end (not modelled). From one wide-angle Mapillary view from the south pavement; positions corrected for a ~20 degree compass error."
